      "text": "1162(ish): Temüjin born (later Genghis Khan)\n  1206: Kurultai — all Mongol tribes unite under Temüjin\n        Title: Genghis Khagan (Universal Ruler)\n  1215: Zhongdu (Beijing) falls — Jin Dynasty crumbling\n  1219–1221: Central Asia (Khwarazmian Empire) destroyed\n  1227: Genghis Khan dies at ~65\n  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n  1229: Ögedei elected Great Khan\n  1234: Jin Dynasty fully conquered\n  1241: Batu/Subutai in Poland + Hungary\n  1258: Hulagu sacks Baghdad; last Abbasid caliph killed\n  1260: Ain Jalut — first major Mongol defeat\n  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n  FOUR KHANATES (after ~1260):\n  +──────────────────────────────────────────────+\n  | YUAN DYNASTY       | CHAGATAI KHANATE        |\n  | (China + Mongolia) | (Central Asia)          |\n  | Kublai Khan        | Endless civil wars      |\n  | → Sinicized        | → Islamized eventually  |\n  +────────────────────+─────────────────────────+\n  | ILKHANATE          | GOLDEN HORDE             |\n  | (Persia/Iraq)      | (Steppe + Russia)        |\n  | Hulagu line        | Batu line                |\n  | → Islamized 1295   | → Islamized ~1313        |\n  +────────────────────+─────────────────────────+\n  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n  1368: Yuan expelled from China → Ming Dynasty\n  1370s: Timur (Tamerlane) begins; Timurid successor\n  ~1380+: Successor khanates fragment\n  1480: Moscow throws off Golden Horde\n  1502: Last Golden Horde Khan defeated\n```"
